tools/SSMFlagbyteDefinitions_en.cpp
forum_full_thread.txt
subaru_5eat_service_manual.pdf
subaru_5eat_service_manual_extract.txt

# Edited ROMs — don't commit work-in-progress tunes
*_edited.bin
*_modified.bin

# Full disassembly listings: ~38 MB per image, 340 MB for the family. Regenerate
# with tools/ghidra/DensoDisasmAll.java; the script is what is worth keeping.
# disasm-denso/ was excluded as "~300 MB of generated listings". It is 34 MB in
# one file - the figure was asserted, never measured. Under GitHub's 100 MB per
# file limit, smaller than the decompiler output already here, and fourteen tools
# need it. Published.

# Build output
build/

# Denso decompiler output is regenerated by tools/ghidra/decompile_all_denso.sh.
# Committed when a run completes; the coverage log is what matters between runs.
decompiled-denso/*.c.tmp

# Regenerable from the listing, and documented as such in
# docs/RUNNING-THE-TOOLS.md. Committing it would mean a stale copy silently
# disagreeing with the disassembly it was derived from.
tools/denso_callgraph.json

# Written after every one of 1,480 runs during a sweep, so it can never match a
# manifest hashed at any single moment - three CI failures in a row said so. The
# finished result is copied to tools/denso_table_effects.json deliberately, once.
tools/denso_perturb_results.json
